The model adopts a capped supply of exactly 200,000,000 tokens with a low-inflation strategy that avoids aggressive ongoing minting, ensuring sustainability. This mirrors design patterns from Aave (governance-focused with ecosystem reserves) and Compound (incentive alignment via user and team shares), while the heavy LP focus echoes Curve's 62% community liquidity provider allocation to bootstrap pools and yield generation.

Allocations prioritize key stakeholders as specified: 50% to Liquidity Providers to attract deposits for lending pools and reward them with trading fees plus token incentives (targeting the noted 30-50% range and aligning with protocol needs for liquidity); 20% to Governance for token-weighted voting on parameters by participants who stake for power; 20% to Team for ongoing development and interim protocol guidance; and 10% to Treasury for grants, insurance, and backstops under DAO control. 

